  "finalText": "I added Rosa Mendel's two bags to reservation R1042, so she now has 3 checked bags. I charged her $45.00 for them as a single baggage fee.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Bags:** R1042 went from 1 checked bag to 3.\n- **Fee:** one baggage fee of $45.00 on R1042. This is the only charge on the booking, and it had no earlier charges.\n\n**Why she owes $45 and not $120:**\n- She is booked in economy, which comes with 1 free bag. Her silver frequent-flyer status adds a second, so she gets 2 free bags.\n- With 3 bags in total, only 1 is beyond her free allowance. It costs $45, the published price for the first extra bag.\n- The $75 price only applies to a second paid bag, which she doesn't have. So $120 ($45 + $75) would overcharge her.\n\n**What to tell Rosa:** \"Your reservation now has 3 checked bags. Your fare includes 1 free bag and your silver status adds a second, so one of the two new bags is free. The other costs $45. 3 bags is the most a reservation can hold, so you can't add any more.\"\n\n**About the date:** this session says today is 2026-10-05, which would mean her 2026-08-11 SFO→Seattle flight has already gone. The airline system says today is 2026-07-28 and lists the flight as scheduled, so I went with the system's date.\n\nI didn't change anything else on her booking, her passenger record or the flight.",
